# ttychatter.bash changelog
## 0.13.2-bash-only

### Added
- `--search QUERY` command for searching session logs without contacting OpenRouter.
- `--all-sessions` search scope flag.
- Runtime `:search TEXT` command for the current session log.
- Runtime `:search-all TEXT` command for all saved session logs.

### Changed
- Search is implemented with plain shell/grep-style log scanning rather than hidden indexes or databases.

### Documentation
- Updated man page with SEARCH section and runtime search commands.

### Notes
- Search does not send prompts, contact OpenRouter, or consume provider requests.

## 0.13.0-bash-only

### Added
- `--set-api-key` now exposes runtime-only, GPG-encrypted, and plaintext storage choices.
- API-key entry reports `gpg not found` when encrypted storage is unavailable.
- Encrypted API-key saving uses external gpg and API_KEY_GPG_FILE when available.

### Changed
- Plaintext API-key storage now requires explicit selection and confirmation.
- GPG failure no longer falls through to plaintext automatically.

### Documentation
- Updated man page API-key storage section.

## 0.13.0-bash-only

### Added
- GPG encrypted API-key save option in --set-api-key / :set-api-key flow.
- "gpg not found" indication when encrypted storage is unavailable.
- API_KEY_GPG_FILE / OPENROUTER_API_KEY_GPG_FILE documentation in man page.

### Changed
- API-key setup now mirrors the security choices of the ncurses and Python-helper clients.
- Plaintext config storage now appears only after an explicit warning.
- Encrypted save removes old plaintext API-key config entries when successful.

### Documentation
- Updated man page API-key/GPG storage section.
- Expanded comments around dependency-light GPG handling.

## 0.12.0

### Added
- Model favorites/bookmarks command support
- THEME config recognition for line-oriented display styling
- SEND_INPUT config support for enter vs Ctrl+D-style input loops
- CODE_ATTACHMENT_MIN_LINES support so short code blocks can remain inline
- Model favorites file support through MODEL_FAVORITES_FILE

### Changed
- Model sorting can now use saved favorites where supported
- Long code-block extraction is now threshold-controlled
- Bash output styling avoids ANSI escapes when output is piped or loopback is active

### Documentation
- Updated man page with favorites, theme, send input, and code attachment threshold sections
- Updated comments around line-oriented parity with the ncurses client

0.11.0-bash-only
- Added --routers and --model-type model-list filters.
- Added MODEL_TYPE_FILTER config support.
- Added runtime :routers command.
- Added dependency-light router/fixed/free/auto filtering using available model-list columns.
- Updated documentation for OpenRouter router entries.

## 0.10.0-bash-only

### Added
- `--loopback` mode for piping AI responses from an interactive chat to another program.
- `--loopback-file <path>` for appending AI responses to a file.
- LOOPBACK_FILE config support.

### Changed
- In `--loopback` mode, interface text is routed to stderr while clean AI responses are written to stdout.

### Documentation
- Added LOOPBACK OUTPUT documentation to the man page and help text.

## 0.9.0-bash-only

### Added
- Optional GPG-encrypted API-key loading through `api-key.gpg`.
- `API_KEY_GPG_FILE` / `OPENROUTER_API_KEY_GPG_FILE` config key support.
- GPG availability and encrypted-key presence checks in `--doctor`.

### Changed
- API-key loading now checks environment, config, and optional GPG encrypted file while remaining Python-free.

### Documentation
- Updated man page with GPG API-key storage behavior.

### Notes
- GPG support is dependency-light and uses the user's external `gpg` command.
- If gpg is unavailable, the Bash-only client still works with environment or plaintext config API keys.

